UPCOMING EVENTS (1 MINUTE PER PERSON)  {\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fswiss\fprq2\fcharset0 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\colortbl ;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\i\f0\fs22 Councilmember Howorth extended her thanks to all attendees for their understanding and patience with the meeting location in the Police/Fire Conference Room.\line\line Police Chief Rachel Johnson invited the community to attend the Tip-A-Cop fundraiser at Tin Roof Bistro on Wednesday, November 5, 2025, from 5:00 PM to 8:00 PM. Proceeds from the event will benefit local Special Olympics.\cf1\b\i0\line\line\cf0\b0\i Waste Management Recycling Education Representative Bobby Bell announced that, although next week includes the Veterans Day holiday, there will be no interruption to service. Waste collection will proceed as scheduled on Tuesday, November 11, 2025.\line\line Library Manager Cassandra Sargent announced that Kindness Week will begin at the library on Monday, November 10, 2025. She also recognized Native American Heritage Month and invited the community to attend a hands-on workshop on Friday, November 14, 2025, from 4:00 PM to 5:00 PM.\b\line\line\b0 Communications and Civic Engagement Manager Alexandria Latragna invited the community to attend the City\rquote s Veterans Day Ceremony, to be held at Valley Drive and Ardmore Avenue on Tuesday, November 11, 2025, at 11:00 AM.\line\line Councilmember Tarnay announced that, due to the current shutdown of the federal SNAP program, the South Bay Food Initiative is hosting a food drive. Community members are encouraged to donate non-perishable food items, which can be dropped off at Mira Costa High School, Redondo Union High School, and Palos Verdes High School. Donation bins will be located in the school lobbies during regular school hours.\line\line Mayor Pro Tem Franklin invited the community to attend the upcoming 6th Annual VetFest, which will be held at Kinecta Federal Credit Union on Saturday, November 8, 2025, from 12:00 PM to 5:00 PM. The annual VetFest is to honor veterans, first responders, and active military.\line\line\pard Mayor Lesser, on behalf of the Mira Costa Drama Group, announced their fall play titled \ldblquote A Beautiful Day in November on the Banks of the Greatest of the Great Lakes,\rdblquote  to be performed at the Mira Costa High School Small Theatre beginning Friday, November 7, 2025. He also invited the community to attend the inaugural \ldblquote Coffee with the Mayor\rdblquote  event at Metlox Plaza on Friday, November 7, 2025, from 9:00 AM to 10:00 AM.\cf2\i0\f1\par
}


G.. PUBLIC COMMENTS (3 MINUTES PER PERSON)
